From: yaoyuping <yaoyuping@hygon.cn>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:41:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 19/24] step5: optional fp8 for the bf16 dense linears and the
 layer 88-90 MoE

VLLM_HCU_STEP5_FP8_DENSE=1: after loading, the attention qkvg/o and dense-MLP
weights are quantized to fp8 e4m3 per output channel and run through LightOp's
hipBLASLt channel-wise W8A8 GEMM with per-token activation scales (computed in
torch ops so Inductor fuses them into the producer). N is padded to a multiple
of 256 to avoid hipBLASLt's slow path. The shared expert, router, indexer,
eh_proj and lm_head stay bf16.

VLLM_HCU_STEP5_FP8_BF16_MOE=1: the bf16 routed experts of layers 88-90
(compressed-tensors ignore entry) are quantized to fp8 per output channel while
loading, so they use the same fp8 MoE path as the other layers.

bs32 64k/4k, MTP3: decode 1248-1259 -> 1319-1333 tok/s, prefill 11240 ->
11800 tok/s. Prompt NLL 0.6483 -> 0.6487-0.6489, top-1 agreement vs bf16
96.8-96.9% (bf16 run-to-run 97.4%).

